@startuml
title TASK-260712-3d0zgu - Deterministic Parity Scenarios

actor User
participant "Telegram adapter" as Bot
participant "SubmitMedia" as Ingest
participant "Inline transaction" as Inline
participant "Transmission scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "History / Presence" as Views
participant "Shared presentation" as Labels

User -> Bot : voice / audio / document
Bot -> Ingest : bounded, untrusted attachment hints
Ingest --> Bot : ready or exact sanitized failure

alt voice ready, no callback
  Bot -> Inline : commit after_current default\nat trusted acceptance time
  Inline -> Scheduler : schedule immediately
  note right of Scheduler
    Out-of-order processing cannot rewrite FIFO.
    No synthetic callback decision wait exists.
  end note
else valid callback before playback
  User -> Bot : opaque tg1_ callback
  Bot -> Inline : re-resolve actor + exact message
  Inline -> Inline : cancel default + create replacement\nin one writer transaction
  Inline -> Scheduler : one replacement target set
else playback start wins
  User -> Bot : opaque tg1_ callback
  Bot -> Inline : atomic apply
  Inline --> Bot : too_late; no cancellation or replacement
else forged / duplicate / cross-user callback
  User -> Bot : invalid or replayed reference
  Bot -> Inline : authorize + deduplicate
  Inline --> Bot : expired / forbidden / already_applied
end

Scheduler -> Views : exact receipt + current policy result
Views -> Labels : semantic keys and safe human metadata
Labels --> User : same RU meaning as app EN/RU catalog

note bottom
  Mixed capabilities downgrade the whole transmission to after_current
  with mandatory_target_missing_overlay_capability; protocols never split.
end note

@enduml
